1
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Worlds collide.

2
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:42,000
The Flash is a action, science fiction, adventure
film directed by Andy Muschietti.

3
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
When his attempt to save his family inadvertently alters the future, Barry Allen becomes trapped in a
reality in which General Zod has returned and there are no Super Heroes to turn to.

4
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:18,000
In order to save the world that he is in and return to the future that
he knows, Barry's only hope is to race for his life.

5
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
But will making the ultimate sacrifice be enough to reset the universe?

6
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Barry Allen / The Flash, played by Ezra Miller.

7
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Kara Zor-El / Supergirl, played by Sasha Calle.

8
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Bruce Wayne / Batman, played by Michael Keaton.

9
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
General Zod, played by Michael Shannon.

10
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Henry Allen, played by Ron Livingston.

11
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Nora Allen, played by Maribel Verdú.

12
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
The Flash is a 2023 American superhero film based on the DC
Comics character Barry Allen / The Flash.

13
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
Directed by Andy Muschietti from a screenplay by Christina Hodson and a story by the writing team of John Francis Daley
and Jonathan Goldstein alongside Joby Harold, it is the 13th film in the DC Extended Universe (DCEU).

14
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
Ezra Miller stars as Barry Allen, who travels back in time to prevent his
mother's death and becomes stranded in an alternate past.

15
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Sasha Calle also stars in her film debut, alongside Michael Shannon, Ron
Livingston, Maribel Verdú, Kiersey Clemons, Antje Traue, and Michael Keaton.

16
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
Barbara Muschietti and Michael Disco produced the
film for DC Films and Warner Bros.

17
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
Development on a film featuring the Flash began in the late 1980s, with various iterations
planned through 2014, when it was redeveloped for the DCEU and Miller was cast.

18
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
Multiple writers and directors were attached over the following years, with Seth Grahame-Smith, Rick
Famuyiwa, Daley, and Goldstein all departing the project over creative differences with the studios.

19
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
Muschietti and Hodson became involved in July 2019, and
pre-production began in January 2020.

20
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Influenced by the 2011 comic book storyline Flashpoint, the film explores the multiverse and features other DC characters, such as Calle's Supergirl and multiple
versions of Batman, particularly Keaton's portrayal from the films Batman (1989) and Batman Returns (1992), while others were digitally included.

21
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
Filming lasted from April to October 2021 at Warner Bros.

22
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:42,000
Studios Leavesden and on location throughout the United Kingdom.

23
01:50:24,000 --> 01:50:30,000
The film's ending was altered several times during post-production due to
changes in DC's wider plans under different studio leadership.

24
01:55:12,000 --> 01:55:18,000
The Flash premiered at Grauman's Chinese Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on June 12, 2023, and was released in the
United States on June 16, following multiple delays caused by the director changes and the COVID-19 pandemic.

25
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics, who praised its humor, action
sequences, and performances, but criticized the visual effects and third act.

26
02:04:48,000 --> 02:04:54,000
It was also a box-office bomb, grossing $271.4 million
worldwide against a budget of $200–220 million.

27
02:09:36,000 --> 02:09:42,000
Its box office performance was attributed to factors such as Miller's legal issues and controversies, the franchise's imminent
reboot with the DC Universe (DCU), superhero fatigue, and the film's mixed reception and marketing practices.

28
02:14:24,000 --> 02:14:30,000
The film explores themes of secret identity, superhero,
time travel, based on comic, superhuman.

29
02:19:12,000 --> 02:19:18,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
